## Why This Is Asked

Localization testing is essential for global products. This question checks practical ability to verify UI text, locale-sensitive formatting, and fallback behavior without page reloads, plus cross‑viewport validation.

## Key Concepts

- Localization testing
- Dynamic content updates without reload
- Intl Date/Number formatting
- Test data seeding and mocking translation APIs
- Cross-viewport testing (desktop/mobile)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright outline
test('localization flow with es locale', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/translations**', route => route.fulfill({ body: JSON.stringify({
    'explore': 'Explorar',
    'price': 'Precio'
  }) }));
  await page.goto('https://example.com/?locale=es');
  await expect(page.locator('h1')).toHaveText('Explorar');
  // check date/price formatting and locale switch without reload
