## Why This Is Asked

Tests in privacy-preserving analytics must guarantee erasure across all data stores, including caches, materialized views, and backups, while maintaining accurate audit trails for compliance.

## Key Concepts
- DSAR data erasure across microservices
- Event sourcing and tombstone propagation
- Soft vs hard deletes and retention windows
- Cross-region replication and data consistency
- Audit logs and backups scrub policy

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test outline for DSAR flow
test('DSAR end-to-end erasure', async () => {
  seedTestUser();
  ingestEvents();
  triggerDSAR();
  await expect(dataRemovedFromPrimaryDB()).toBe(true);
  await expect(eventStoreHasDeletion()).toBe(true);
  await expect(cacheInvalidated()).toBe(true);
  await expect(auditLogsContain('DSAR')).toBe(true);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate that backups are scrubbed after the retention window without impacting restore capabilities?
- What observability signals would you add to detect DSAR failures in a multi-region deployment?

## Why This Is Asked
Testing offline sync in PWAs is a core beginner task that exercises service workers, local storage, and synchronization logic in a deterministic way.

## Key Concepts
- Service workers offline caching and background sync
- Local storage/state replicas and reconciliation
- Network emulation in tests and deterministic assertions
- Retry patterns to avoid flaky tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright offline-then-online test outline
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('offline note sync', async ({ browser }) => {
  const context = await browser.newContext();
  const page = await context.newPage();
  await context.setOffline(true);
  await page.goto('https://note.example');
  await page.click('#new-note');
  await page.fill('#title','Offline note');
  await page.fill('#content','content');
  await context.setOffline(false);
  await page.waitForResponse(resp => resp.url().includes('/notes') && resp.status() === 200);
  // verify sync and UI badge
  await expect(page.locator('#status')).toHaveText(/Synced/);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for multi-device sync?
- How would you detect and handle merge conflicts during offline edits?

